  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 348 AM EDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\n- Morning Fog\n\nOvernight observations and short term guidance gives fair to good\nconfidence in dense fog Saturday morning throughout much of Mid \nMichigan including along US-127 and reaching portions of US-131. \nThere is some potential for the fog to expand west of US-131 \nmainly west of Kalamazoo and Grand Rapids. Similar to a couple \nother fog events this week, the most widespread visibilities less \nthan a quarter mile may occur between 8 AM and 10 AM when the \nwinds around 500 feet relax. The fog and low clouds should mix out\nand evaporate between 10 AM and noon, leaving the rest of the day\nwith some cirrus.\n\n- Warm Weekend\n\nGlobal ensemble systems and recent short term guidance continues \nstrong support for highs in the upper 60s to around 70 this \nweekend, with a flow of mild air on the back side of high pressure\nover the Northeast to Ohio valley. A light breeze and some \nincreased coverage of high clouds can also be expected.\n\n- Cooler Monday-Tuesday\n\nEnsemble spread has tightened up a little on cooler temperatures \nMonday and Tuesday as a cold front sinks through the area. There \nis still some spread in the expected highs with a range between \nthe mid 50s and mid 60s, depending the southward progress the \nfront makes before stalling. This cool down isn't exactly \nsignificant as it just brings temperatures closer to normal for \nlate October. The front is also favored to come through dry.\n\n- Unsettled End of October\n\nEnsembles have a good signal for high temperatures rebounding \ninto the 60s to near 70 on Wednesday ahead of a northern Plains \nlow. After Wednesday, there was a significant amount of spread and\nlower confidence in the forecast depending on how that low would \nphase with the northern jet stream, and at what longitude a large \nscale trough within the northern stream would set up later in the \nweek. There was a variety of solutions for late in the week with \nhighs ranging between the 40s to near 70, however, recent cycles \nhave increased the membership of warmer solutions. There are \nincreasing chances for rain toward the end of the month, though \nconfidence in that remains relatively low for now.",
